Description: Provides reproducible computational tools for occupational noise
    exposure assessment and spatial noise modelling. The package implements
    logarithmic sound-level addition, daily and weekly exposure calculations,
    noise dose and maximum admissible exposure time, hearing-protector
    calculations using APV, HML and SNR approaches, and regulatory assessment
    helpers using Spanish Real Decreto 286/2006 and European Directive
    2003/10/EC terminology. It also provides free-field propagation,
    barrier-aware receiver calculations, spatial noise grids, noise contours,
    approximate reverberation modelling and inverse estimation of source
    levels. A Shiny application is included for interactive occupational-noise
    calculations and mapping workflows, while the calculation core remains
    independently callable and unit tested. User-facing messages and the
    interactive application support both Spanish and English through a shared
    internationalisation layer.
